:{"provider":"call_S6C1kIYcaLj3VhkPJcJaiIYl"},"name":"search_world","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Bren Vale (person) [ID: 3866be6c-f8eb-4158-8abb-a95e3ddc64b2] [Aliases: Captain]: Bren Vale captains the fishing boat Petrel. People on the dock also call him Captain. He is unrelated to Asha Pell and is not a member of the Lantern Guild.\n  Properties: source_conversation: 01a18769-1953-7785-bf1a-1d436775cbaf\n  - CAPTAINS → Petrel (boat, fishing boat) [ID: 3f555d2a-f6ee-476b-93e5-79e9ae67c110]: A fishing boat captained by Bren Vale.\n  - UNRELATED_TO → Asha Pell (person) [ID: 5affd0ca-9c42-4463-bed7-ad12e3c38d62] [Aliases: Captain Ash]: Asha Pell captains the courier ship Nightjar, grew up in Vesper, and belongs to the Lantern Guild. Her crew usually calls her Captain Ash. She has a small brass key sewn inside her left coat cuff; only her navigator, Iven Marr, knows she has it.\n  - NOT_MEMBER_OF → Lantern Guild (guild) [ID: a4140448-57b9-47e2-9fad-b44a4a957bdd]: Maintains Vesper's tidal lighthouse and buys blue salt from Orin's miners. It does not own the mines. During winter, when the strait freezes, the guild uses stored salt.\n\nPetrel (boat, fishing boat) [ID: 3f555d2a-f6ee-476b-93e5-79e9ae67c110]: A fishing boat captained by Bren Vale.\n  Properties: source_conversation: 01a18769-1953-7785-bf1a-1d436775cbaf\n  - ← CAPTAINS from Bren Vale (person) [ID: 3866be6c-f8eb-4158-8abb-a95e3ddc64b2] [Aliases: Captain]: Bren Vale captains the fishing boat Petrel. People on the dock also call him Captain. He is unrelated to Asha Pell and is not a member of the Lantern Guild.\n\nLantern Guild (guild) [ID: a4140448-57b9-47e2-9fad-b44a4a957bdd]: Maintains Vesper's tidal lighthouse and buys blue salt from Orin's miners. It does not own the mines. During winter, when the strait freezes, the guild uses stored salt.\n  Properties: source_conversation: 01a18769-1953-7785-bf1a-1d436775cbaf\n  - ← MAINTAINED_BY from Vesper lighthouse (lighthouse, landmark) [ID: 18f09cc9-0d1f-4860-a786-04aae26429af]: The tidal lighthouse around which Vesper is built. Its lenses run on blue salt and it is maintained by the Lantern Guild.\n  - ← MEMBER_OF from Asha Pell (person) [ID: 5affd0ca-9c42-4463-bed7-ad12e3c38d62] [Aliases: Captain Ash]: Asha Pell captains the courier ship Nightjar, grew up in Vesper, and belongs to the Lantern Guild. Her crew usually calls her Captain Ash. She has a small brass key sewn inside her left coat cuff; only her navigator, Iven Marr, knows she has it.\n  - ← NOT_MEMBER_OF from Bren Vale (person) [ID: 3866be6c-f8eb-4158-8abb-a95e3ddc64b2] [Aliases: Captain]: Bren Vale captains the fishing boat Petrel. People on the dock also call him Captain. He is unrelated to Asha Pell and is not a member of the Lantern Guild.\n  - ← HONORS_CIVILIAN_CONTRACTS_WITH from Sera Dain (person) [ID: 3bc5f9a9-a1a4-4886-8445-bbff1e085eba]: Leader of the Deep Bell Union. She refuses to sell salt to the military but honors civilian contracts with the Lantern Guild.\n  - BUYS_FROM → Orin's miners (miners, group) [ID: 01f68fd0-b24a-490d-86d5-43195a8bd524]: Miners on Orin who mine blue salt; the Lantern Guild buys salt from them. They formed the Deep Bell Union.\n  - USES → Blue salt (mineral, resource) [ID: a904844d-81e0-40dd-9f91-77fbdc115adb]: Salt used to power the lenses of Vesper's lighthouse; mined on the island of Orin.\n\nVesper lighthouse (lighthouse, landmark) [ID: 18f09cc9-0d1f-4860-a786-04aae26429af]: The tidal lighthouse around which Vesper is built. Its lenses run on blue salt and it is maintained by the Lantern Guild.\n  Properties: source_conversation: 01a18769-1953-7785-bf1a-1d436775cbaf\n  - ← LOCATED_BENEATH from Old lens room (room, location) [ID: 6f9156cc-d754-4aa5-b17d-828367571776]: A room beneath Vesper's lighthouse, opened by Asha Pell's small brass key.\n  - LOCATED_IN → Vesper (city, port city) [ID: ccb13663-df18-4e63-b89c-006464a6cfb2]: Brinewake's main port city, built around a tidal lighthouse.\n  - MAINTAINED_BY → Lantern Guild (guild) [ID: a4140448-57b9-47e2-9fad-b44a4a957bdd]: Maintains Vesper's tidal lighthouse and buys blue salt from Orin's miners. It does not own the mines. During winter, when the strait freezes, the guild uses stored salt.\n  - USES → Blue salt (mineral, resource) [ID: a904844d-81e0-40dd-9f91-77fbdc115adb]: Salt used to power the lenses of Vesper's lighthouse; mined on the island of Orin.\n\nOrin's mines (mines) [ID: 623be29f-ae99-4f3a-b37e-8ee2e0ff0cd4]: Mines on the island of Orin. The Lantern Guild does not own them; it buys blue salt from Orin's miners.\n  Properties: source_conversation: 01a18769-1953-7785-bf1a-1d436775cbaf\n  - ← WORKS_IN from Orin's miners (miners, group) [ID: 01f68fd0-b24a-490d-86d5-43195a8bd524]: Miners on Orin who mine blue salt; the Lantern Guild buys salt from them. They formed the Deep Bell Union.\n  - LOCATED_IN → Orin (island) [ID: 31795bd3-db8b-4121-a619-b483ad06b17a]: An island where blue salt is mined by its miners."}]}]},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"reasoning","text":"**Considering political dynamics**\n\nI need to craft a concise response that engages with the political context, possibly contrasting the positions of Bren and the Lantern Guild. It seems important to note Bren's support for peers versus the Guild's supply costs. I should clarify whether the toll affects all blue salt shipments or just those coming into Vesper, especially since the newly stated focus is on shipments. I don't want to repeat previous searches, but I can highlight Bren's position despite him not being a Guild member.","native":{"item":{"reasoning":"**Considering political dynamics**\n\nI need to craft a concise response that engages with the political context, possibly contrasting the positions of Bren and the Lantern Guild. It seems important to note Bren's support for peers versus the Guild's supply costs. I should clarify whether the toll affects all blue salt shipments or just those coming into Vesper, especially since the newly state